  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manas Kumar Jena vs State Of Odisha .... Opposite Parties on 12 January, 2026 Author: V. Narasingh Bench: V. Narasingh In The High Court Of Orissa At Cuttack W.P.(C) No.285 of 2026 Manas Kumar Jena .... Petitioner Mr. P. K. Satapathy, Advocate -versus- 1. State of Odisha .... Opposite Parties 2. Collector, Sundargarh 3. Sundargarh Municipality, represented through its Chairman, Sundargarh Municipality office 4. Executive Officer, Sundargarh Municipality 5 . Tahasildar, Sundargarh 6. Iic, Sundargarh Town Police Station Mr. M. R. Mohanty, Aga Coram: Justice V. Narasingh Order Order No. 12.01.2026 01. 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. It is submitted by the learned counsel that the Petitioner has a Food vending establishment in the name and style of Hotel Manshika for which he was granted Trade License by the Sundergarh Municipality as well as the certificate under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Notwithstanding the same, he is facing imminent threat of eviction which according to the Petitioner is clear violation of the prescribed norms inasmuch as no notice has been given to him. 4. It is further submitted by the learned counsel on instruction that the Petitioner can be suitably adjusted without affecting the road expansion work.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. It is submitted by the learned counsel that the Petitioner has a Food vending establishment in the name and style of Hotel Manshika for which he was granted Trade License by the Sundergarh Municipality as well as the certificate under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Notwithstanding the same, he is facing imminent threat of eviction which according to the Petitioner is clear violation of the prescribed norms inasmuch as no notice has been given to him. 4. It is further submitted by the learned counsel on instruction that the Petitioner can be suitably adjusted without affecting the road expansion work.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
